) | [x] |\n| R07 | `run` (FFI) | `bathrooms` = near-tie decimals whose nearest double falls just below/above `x.x5`: `0.05, 0.15, 0.25, 0.35, 0.45, …, 2.05, 8.3, 1.15, 0.145, 4.35` | [x] |\n| R08 | `run` (FFI) | `bathrooms ∈ {0.0, -0.0}` (sign of zero must survive `%.1f` and `+= 1.0`) | [x] |\n| R09 | `run` (FFI) | `bathrooms ∈ {+Inf, -Inf, NaN, -NaN, NaN with payload, signalling NaN}` | [x] |\n| R10 | `run` (FFI) | `bathrooms` subnormal / tiny: `5e-324`, `-5e-324`, `2.2250738585072014e-308`, `±1e-300`, `±1e-16` | [x] |\n| R11 | `run` (FFI) | `bathrooms` large: `2⁵³/10` neighbourhood (`9.007199254740992e14 ± ulp`), `1e15`, `2⁵³`, `1e16`, `1e300`, `DBL_MAX`, and the negatives of each | [x] |\n| R12 | `run` (FFI) | `bathrooms` where `+= 1.0` is lossy or saturating: `2⁵³`, `2⁵³-1`, `2⁵²+0.5`, `1e16`, `DBL_MAX`, `-1.0`, `-0.5` | [x] |\n| R13 | `run` (FFI) | 4096 uniformly random *bit patterns* for `bathrooms` × random `floors`/`bedrooms`/`extra` (includes NaNs/Inf/subnormals) | [x] |\n| R14 | `run` (FFI) | 4096 random \"mixed\" doubles (quarters, tenths, ×10^±k, huge integers) × random ints | [x] |\n| R15 | `run` (FFI) | two consecutive `run` calls on the same struct (what `main` does) for every special `bathrooms` value of R06–R12 | [x] |\n| M01 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | plain non-negative decimal: `\"0\\n\"`, `\"7\\n\"`, `\"12345\\n\"`, `\"2147483646\\n\"` | [x] |\n| M02 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | explicit sign: `\"-7\\n\"`, `\"+7\\n\"`, `\"-0\\n\"`, `\"+0\\n\"` | [x] |\n| M03 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | leading whitespace classes accepted by `strtol`: `\" 7\\n\"`, `\"\\t7\\n\"`, `\"\\v7\\n\"`, `\"\\f7\\n\"`, `\"\\r7\\n\"`, `\"\\n7\\n\"` (first line empty → rejection), mixtures, whitespace + sign | [x] |\n| M04 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | leading zeros: `\"007\\n\"`, `\"0000000000000000000000000007\\n\"`, 90 zeros + `\"7\\n\"`, `\"-007\\n\"` | [x] |\n| M05 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | trailing garbage after a valid prefix: `\"7abc\\n\"`, `\"7 8\\n\"`, `\"7.9\\n\"`, `\"0x10\\n\"`, `\"7e3\\n\"`, `\"12,34\\n\"`, `\"5-\\n\"` | [x] |\n| M06 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | no trailing newline (`\"7\"`, `\"-7\"`, `\"abc\"`, `\"\"`) — `fgets` stops at EOF | [x] |\n| M07 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | empty stdin (0 bytes) → `fgets` returns NULL, buffer stays `\"\"` | [x] |\n| M08 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | newline-only / blank first line (`\"\\n\"`, `\"\\n7\\n\"`, `\"\\r\\n\"`) | [x] |\n| M09 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | `int` boundaries exactly: `\"2147483647\\n\"`, `\"-2147483648\\n\"`, `\"2147483646\\n\"`, `\"-2147483647\\n\"` | [x] |\n| M10 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | between `int` and `long`: `\"2147483648\\n\"`, `\"-2147483649\\n\"`, `\"4294967296\\n\"`, `\"9223372036854775807\\n\"` | [x] |\n| M11 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | beyond `long` (ERANGE): `\"9223372036854775808\\n\"`, `\"-9223372036854775809\\n\"`, 30/60/98/99 digit numbers, `\"1\"` + 98 zeros | [x] |\n| M12 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | line length vs the 99-byte `fgets` cap: 97, 98, 99, 100, 101, 150 bytes, both digits-only and digits + padding, with and without `\\n` at the cut point | [x] |\n| M13 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | multi-line stdin — only the first line may be consumed (`\"7\\n9\\n\"`, `\"abc\\n7\\n\"`, 100 lines) | [x] |\n| M14 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | embedded NUL bytes (`\"\\0\"`, `\"\\0007\\n\"`, `\"7\\0 9\\n\"`, `\"12\\0\"`) | [x] |\n| M15 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | non-UTF-8 / high bytes (`0xFF`, `0x80`, `0xC3 0x28`, byte 0x00–0xFF sweep prefixes) | [x] |\n| M16 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | CRLF and lone CR (`\"7\\r\\n\"`, `\"7\\r\"`, `\"\\r7\\n\"`) | [x] |\n| M17 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | oversized stdin: 100 KiB single line, 100 KiB with no newline, 100 KiB of whitespace | [x] |\n| M18 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | 512 random byte strings (length 0–120, alphabet biased to digits/signs/whitespace/garbage) | [x] |\n| M19 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | 1024 random decimal texts around the `int`/`long` boundaries (`±(2³¹±δ)`, `±(2⁶³±δ)`, random 1–40 digit numbers, random `i64`/`i32` values) | [x] |\n| M20 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | whitespace-only lines of every whitespace class and length (1–99 chars) | [x] |\n| M21 | `main` (FFI) + both exes | valid number split by the 99-byte cap, i.e. padding then digits crossing the boundary (`\" \"×90 + \"1234567890123\"`) | [x] |\n\nBoth `.so`s' `main` is additionally checked to return the same `int` (always 0)\nand to terminate the same way (same exit status, no signal), and both\nexecutables are checked for identical stderr (always empty) and exit status.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
