{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bv5rjhd5bewaqm5x6r26asfyrxltmmtirwy6pukymehbps4gzrna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and the work uncovered and fixed two real divergences.\n\n## What this project actually is\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` builds an **executable** (82-line single translation unit), and `Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]`** — so the feature enumeration is `{default}` ≡ `{--no-default-features}` ≡ `{--all-features}` (all three are still run, so it's verified, not assumed), crossed with `{dev, release}` profiles.\n\nTo compare through the FFI boundary as required, I compiled the same C translation unit into `c_build/libcdriver.so` (without touching `c_src/`) and restructured the Rust crate so it produces **both** the `driver` binary and a `cdylib` exporting the identical C-ABI surface: `src/imp.rs` (translation), `src/main.rs` (binary), `src/lib.rs` (`cdylib` exporting `run` + `main`). Tests only ever reach Rust via `dlopen`/`dlsym` or by spawning the executable.\n\n## Phase A artifacts\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | C `.so` defines exactly `main`, `run`; Rust `.so` defines exactly `main`, `run`. **Symbol diff empty**, no non-libc undefined symbols (`ldd -r` clean). `check_symbols.sh` re-checks mechanically. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 21 rows, grep-derived: the 4 independent conditions of the single `parse_val` guard, the ignored `fgets` return, the 99-byte truncation, embedded NUL, unchecked/NULL/misaligned pointer, both signed-overflow spots, SIGPIPE, EBADF stdin. All `[x]`. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 8 branch axes → 48 rows (17 `run` rows, 26 stdin rows, 5 exhaustive sweeps). All `[x]`. |\n\n## Divergences found and fixed\n1. **`run(NULL, x)`**: C died with SIGSEGV, debug-Rust aborted (SIGABRT) because `&mut *ptr` trips Rust's null check → export now uses `ptr::read`/`ptr::write` (faults like C; misaligned pointers also behave like C).\n2. **SIGPIPE**: with stdout a pipe with no reader, the C driver was killed by signal 13 while Rust exited 0 (Rust's runtime sets `SIG_IGN`) → `src/main.rs` records the *inherited* disposition in an ELF `.init_array` constructor and restores it, so it now dies (or doesn't) exactly when C does.\n3. `[lib] test = false` so `cargo test` can link (the cdylib exports a C-ABI `main`).\n\n## Evidence\n- 82 tests × 4 build configurations, 0 failures (`./verify.sh` → `ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED`).\n- ~1.5 M differential comparisons in the normal suite (48 K + 110 K randomized/structured `run` cases, ~6 300 exhaustive stdin enumerations incl. all 4096 three-byte strings), plus a one-off heavy pass of ~1.05 M more.\n- Harness **mutation-tested**: `{:.1}`→`{:.2}` failed 10/15 rows; perturbing the fast path failed 15/15 — both formatter paths are genuinely observed.\n- Two adversarial audits (independent glibc reference programs, ~69 M and ~280 M value comparisons) found **no divergence**; every candidate they produced is now a passing regression test in `tests/audit_regressions.rs`. Their one substantive finding was an inaccurate code comment, which I corrected."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":255042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":649,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3474c86-67f7-4839-840d-8be73b7aa864","uuid":"6df6f7e6-8f6a-4dd2-bc38-bc8d04caaef9","timestamp":"2026-08-18T05:11:44.483Z"}
